{"schema":1,"kind":"decision","id":"01KZBAPJNAGEN79FRJHXSZF2C7","title":"Heredoc bodies are data: mask them before deriving capabilities","decision":"Mask heredoc bodies out of the segment/substitution/redirect scans, gated by a data-consumer allowlist plus an interpreter denylist, and leave unterminated heredocs untouched.","alternatives":[{"option":"Interpreter denylist only (mask unless the line names bash/sh/ssh/...)","why_rejected":"fails open on any consumer we forgot to list; an unlisted executor would silently hide live code from the hard stops"},{"option":"Fix only the per-line regex anchor in the YAML extractor","why_rejected":"treats the symptom for one rule and leaves every other capability derived from heredoc prose, including the compiled hard stops"},{"option":"Document the trap in AGENT_CONTEXT.md and require --body-file","why_rejected":"keeps punishing the act of writing a warning down, and relies on every agent remembering prose"}],"scope":["crates/gommage-core/src/shell.rs,crates/gommage-core/src/mapper.rs"],"commits":["3a7e4444ad891a909c40d274f957fb7a21977bf0"],"author":"codex","confidence":"medium","tags":[],"ts":1786012977834}
